Over in src/distrib/alpha/floppy-GENERIC you will see a setup that does
everything for you. I think it's actually borked right now on the exact
GENERIC kernel, because it overflowed the floppy, but you should have
no trouble at all if you either point it at a custom Multia kernel
(that has most of the random drivers removed) or if you trim down
your GENERIC config.

